From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:32:10 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] crash-guard

slot writes Config/starting.txt (platform and stem) before it opens a
core, and removes it once the game has published 300 frames or a
resume state is written (flush, autosave). A boot that finds the mark
naming the cart it would put back leaves that cart selected on the
shelf with a Last start failed banner, so a game that crashes while
starting no longer crashes every boot. The resume state stays on the
card. Upstream-first (ADR 0047, ADR 0084): drop this patch when the
upstream PR lands. Idea from oauramos/omega-zero be6eb11.
